## For years, founders have fallen into the same simple, costly trap

They try to market to everyone. In the early stages of building a lead generation engine, it's incredibly easy to tell yourself your market is huge, that you target founders, CXOs, and mid-sized B2B business owners. It sounds focused, right? But the reality is that targeting an audience that broad is essentially praying in the dark.

## Confession number one: 15 years of lead generation mistakes

When Myntmore's founder, Tejas Jhaveri, looked back at 15 years of lead generation mistakes, this was confession number one: reaching out to broad, vague categories before truly understanding the Ideal Customer Profile (ICP). If you try to speak to every founder or CXO with the same generic messaging, your lead generation funnel will always feel random, unpredictable, and entirely dependent on luck.

## Stop chasing a massive, theoretical market

To build a B2B system that consistently books 35 to 60 highly qualified meetings every single month, you have to stop chasing a massive, theoretical market. You need to transition from your Total Addressable Market to what's actually in front of you right now:

We map your real, reachable market and score the accounts in it; see our [ICP mapping and lead scoring service](/services/sales-intelligence).

- Total Addressable Market (TAM): the broad, high-level audience that theoretically could buy your product in a perfect world.
- Total Conversional Market (TCM): the highly specific, highly motivated subset of prospects who are actively feeling the pain point today, are already looking for workarounds, and are ready to act immediately.

## When you target your TCM, everything changes

Your product is no longer a generic suggestion. It sits right in the middle of a priority they are already trying to solve. Great B2B positioning survives non-experts because it is simple, clear, and focused on one specific customer living with one specific, painful problem. If your pipeline is currently full of polite "maybe later" responses, that's a clear sign your ICP is still too vague. To address high-value target accounts with pinpoint precision, explore our [account-based marketing service](/services/account-based-marketing), or see how we tailor messaging for specialized sectors like [IT firms and digital agencies](/lp/agencies-it).
